<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundle's Info.plist by Tauri, which picks up any Info.plist
  sitting next to tauri.conf.json.

  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription is not optional: macOS terminates a process that
  touches the microphone without one, so its absence is a crash on first
  dictation rather than a missing prompt.

  NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription is the same kind of key for Bluetooth: the
  connect notifications and device list (IOBluetooth) are covered by the
  Bluetooth privacy permission on macOS 11 and later.

  NSRemindersFullAccessUsageDescription is what EventKit's full-access request
  (macOS 14+) needs to read reminders in process. Without the key the request
  is a kill, so the agenda crate checks for it before asking and otherwise
  reads through scripting.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Aloud records your voice so it can transcribe what you say and paste the text into the app you are using.</string>
    <key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Aloud notices when your headphones connect or disconnect, and when a device's battery is running low, so it can tell you in the notch.</string>
    <key>NSRemindersFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Aloud shows the reminders that are due or overdue in the notch, and notices when one comes due.</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
